    "summary": "Smoking Crazy Fingers, thunderous Cold Rain > Samson, epic Other One",
    "blurb": "The July 29‑1982 Red Rocks set shines with a searing Crazy Fingers and a ferocious Cold Rain And Snow → Samson transition. The second set builds into an expansive Other One that rides Phil’s booming bass and Bill’s high‑energy drumming. Overall the show is a high‑octane, rain‑slick performance captured well on several audience tapes.",
    "review": "What unfolds at Red Rocks on July 29, 1982 finds the Dead firing on all cylinders despite a drizzle soaking the amphitheatre. The first set eases in with New Minglewood Blues and a soulful Feel Like A Stranger before gathering momentum into a thunderous Cold Rain And Snow that segues straight into Samson & Delilah – a moment where Jerry’s guitar is described as “smoking” and Phil’s bass ramps into a powerful crescendo that fuels the ensuing jam. Crazy Fingers erupts with crystalline leads, while I Need A Miracle launches an inventive G‑jam that rolls into a sprawling Other One, highlighted by Bill Kreutzmann’s explosive drum break and a soaring bass line that drives the improvisation to its climax. The encore’s Brokedown Palace provides a gentle wind‑down after a night of high‑octane interplay, making this Red Rocks gig one of the most memorable shows of the 1982 summer run.",
